     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"With no defences the attacker wins: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, then pivot_internal gives reach_internal (not segmented), then auth_appserver (MFA bypassed from the workstation), then kerberoast gives stolen_admin, then auth_dc, escalate_dc and dump_dbadmin_dc give stolen_dbadmin, and that leads to the db, fileserver or backup and exfiltration. So zero controls is not enough. Every exfiltration path needs admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup. Each of these needs foothold_db, foothold_fileserver or foothold_backup, which need stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs. These need admin_dc or admin_adfs, which need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs. Those footholds come only from auth_dc or auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore cuts every path, so the minimum is 1.\"}"
